{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/the-history-of-wedding-food/audio/main-818cd81978a7.mp3","durationSec":194.232,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3,"text":"Wedding food can show social rank as well as celebration."},{"start":3.58,"end":10.02,"text":"In ancient Rome, confarreatio, which literally meant \"with spelt,\" was a patrician form of marriage."},{"start":10.52,"end":14.38,"text":"The bride and groom shared spelt cake and bread during the ceremony."},{"start":14.82,"end":21.8,"text":"Because patricians belonged to Rome's upper class, this simple grain food carried legal, religious, and social meaning."},{"start":22.3,"end":28.06,"text":"Records of medieval French feasts help us understand how a noble wedding banquet could make status visible."},{"start":28.52,"end":32.34,"text":"Aristocratic tables might offer peacock, heron, or swan."},{"start":32.72,"end":39.78,"text":"Imported spices such as saffron, ginger, nutmeg, cardamom, and cinnamon came from far-off places."},{"start":40.4,"end":45.04,"text":"They were rare and valuable, so serving them showed a host's wealth and trade connections."},{"start":45.6,"end":51.06,"text":"Even the seating could show rank: the most important guest sat nearest the large salt container."},{"start":51.06,"end":57.16,"text":"Wedding food was not only a meal; ingredients and presentation helped families show their place in society."},{"start":57.9,"end":60.74,"text":"Religious wedding food does not follow one universal menu."},{"start":61.14,"end":63.56,"text":"It changes by region, community, and family."},{"start":64.22,"end":70.18,"text":"At one Hindu wedding described by Smithsonian, the bride received a coconut, which the couple then gave to the groom."},{"start":70.84,"end":75.08,"text":"The coconut was a divine offering for a blessed marriage and a symbol of prosperity."},{"start":75.76,"end":80.46,"text":"A paste of cumin seeds and brown sugar represented the bitter and sweet parts of life."},{"start":81.08,"end":84.84,"text":"Rice also appeared as a symbol of sustenance and as an offering."},{"start":85.76,"end":87.46,"text":"Jewish weddings offer another example."},{"start":88.34,"end":93.12,"text":"Blessings over wine are part of the ceremony, and the couple drinks from a cup after the seven blessings."},{"start":93.8,"end":100.32,"text":"The feast afterwards is called a seudat mitzvah, a religiously important meal with food, dancing, and singing."},{"start":100.32,"end":103.22,"text":"Guests are encouraged to help the couple rejoice."},{"start":103.96,"end":107.58,"text":"The exact dishes vary, but the shared meal has a clear purpose."},{"start":108.2,"end":114.72,"text":"In both traditions, food turns belief into something families and guests can see, taste, and take part in."},{"start":115.14,"end":117.46,"text":"The wedding cake changed over many centuries."},{"start":118.12,"end":123.62,"text":"In seventeenth-century England, a bride cake was closer to sweet bread with fruit and spices."},{"start":124.56,"end":128.6,"text":"By the eighteenth century, fruit cakes were often covered with sugar icing."},{"start":128.6,"end":135.26,"text":"Whiter icing required better, more expensive sugar, so its color became a sign of money."},{"start":135.9,"end":147,"text":"At Queen Victoria and Prince Albert's wedding in 1840, the cake weighed 136 kilograms, measured about 2.7 metres around, and had detailed figures on top."},{"start":147.68,"end":150.32,"text":"It made royal extravagance easy to see."},{"start":151.04,"end":159.02,"text":"Later royal cakes became taller and more complex, and smaller, cheaper versions reached more families near the end of Victoria's reign."},{"start":159.58,"end":161.68,"text":"Tradition does not always mean cake."},{"start":162.3,"end":169.58,"text":"In Uzbekistan, plov is a national rice-and-meat dish served at weddings, births, funerals, and holidays."},{"start":170.54,"end":174.64,"text":"Wedding plov may include extra chickpeas, raisins, and garlic."},{"start":175.4,"end":179.4,"text":"A skilled cook can prepare one huge pot for hundreds of guests."},{"start":180.4,"end":183.84,"text":"Plov shows family memory, hospitality, and community."},{"start":184.16,"end":193.92,"text":"Together, the white cake and communal plov show two paths: wedding food can display wealth, or it can make an old shared dish feel especially joyful."}],"words":[{"text":"Wedding","start":0,"end":0.36},{"text":"food","start":0.36,"end":0.7},{"text":"can","start":0.7,"end":0.94},{"text":"show","start":0.94,"end":1.2},{"text":"social","start":1.2,"end":1.62},{"text":"rank","start":1.62,"end":1.92},{"text":"as","start":1.92,"end":2.18},{"text":"well","start":2.18,"end":2.38},{"text":"as","start":2.38,"end":2.56},{"text":"celebration","start":2.56,"end":3},{"text":"In","start":3.58,"end":3.72},{"text":"ancient","start":3.72,"end":4.02},{"text":"Rome","start":4.02,"end":4.36},{"text":"confarreatio","start":4.36,"end":5.92},{"text":"which","start":5.92,"end":6.24},{"text":"literally","start":6.24,"end":6.82},{"text":"meant","start":6.82,"end":7.2},{"text":"with","start":7.2,"end":7.46},{"text":"spelt","start":7.46,"end":7.86},{"text":"was","start":8.32,"end":8.64},{"text":"a","start":8.64,"end":8.78},{"text":"patrician","start":8.78,"end":9.2},{"text":"form","start":9.2,"end":9.46},{"text":"of","start":9.46,"end":9.64},{"text":"marriage","start":9.64,"end":10.02},{"text":"The","start":10.52,"end":10.76},{"text":"bride","start":10.76,"end":11.1},{"text":"and","start":11.1,"end":11.4},{"text":"groom","start":11.4,"end":11.7},{"text":"shared","start":11.7,"end":12.1},{"text":"spelt","start":12.1,"end":12.52},{"text":"cake","start":12.52,"end":12.8},{"text":"and","start":12.8,"end":13.14},{"text":"bread","start":13.14,"end":13.44},{"text":"during","start":13.44,"end":13.78},{"text":"the","start":13.78,"end":13.96},{"text":"ceremony","start":13.96,"end":14.38},{"text":"Because","start":14.82,"end":15.08},{"text":